    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the slate with a high-upside core, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (71.62), who boasts the highest efficiency score of the day. Despite a neutral park, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start due to his elite 0.452 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Davis Martin. Joining him as a primary engine is **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (68.40), who benefits significantly from a park factor boost (+14%) and a soft matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano (4.89 xERA), positioning him as the day\u2019s most potent value play. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (66.29) remains vital for our pursuit of the stolen base category; despite facing a tough arm in Jacob Misiorowski, his leadoff spot and a +14% platoon edge against a right-handed pitcher solidify his role as a critical daily contributor.\n\nStrategy for the middle infield highlights the importance of matching our aggressive base-stealing philosophy against favorable game conditions. **Trea Turner** (66.93) continues to lead our roster in reliability, while **Colt Keith** (59.29) earns a start through a strong order placement and platoon advantage, despite the marginal suppression of his efficiency by Dean Kremer\u2019s ability to hold runners. The tightest decision on the bench involved **Chase Meidroth** (44.27); he was the closest consideration for a starting spot, but his bottom-third placement in the batting order and a lack of elite speed compared to our rostered outfielders kept him behind the current starters. We are closely monitoring the lineups for **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, and **Kazuma Okamoto**, as their status remains pending; should any move down the order, we will reassess our game-cap preservation strategy for the late-season push.",
